## Scope
Review the pull request for correctness, regressions, maintainability, compatibility with the surrounding code, and missing tests. Prioritize concrete findings with file and line references. Verify the PR title and body against the diff and relevant neighboring code.

Run or inspect the most relevant tests when feasible. Do not rewrite the implementation unless the task explicitly asks for direct fixes.

## Submit
Write the PR review summary to `{output_target}`. Lead with findings by severity, then list open questions, tests checked, and a concise verdict.

## Submit formal review
After writing `{output_target}`, you MUST submit the formal Forgejo review. This is the deliverable; an artifact file alone is not complete.

Map your final decision to the CLI event: `APPROVED` -> `approved`; any blocking finding or required remediation -> `changes`.

Run this command, replacing `<approved|changes>` with the mapped event and never printing tokens:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  pr-review {forgejo_repo} {pr_number} <approved|changes> "Code Reviewer" --body-file "{output_target}"
```

Then verify the review landed:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  fg-reviews {forgejo_repo} {pr_number}
```

The verification must show a review by the Code Reviewer role identity (`agent-code-reviewer`). Report the review id. If posting or verification fails, treat the run as a hard failure and do not report success.

